---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'What Sameet Sapra is focused on right now: software engineering in Chicago, building with AI agents, writing again, and eating his way through his own map.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Now" description={description}>
  <div class="measure">
    <h1>Now</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p><em>Updated October 2026, from Chicago.</em></p>

      <p>
        I'm a software engineer at Meta, based in Chicago. Most of my
        building energy right now goes two places:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Building with AI agents.</strong> I run much of my
          life admin — and now this entire website — through an AI
          agent I direct. The site you're reading is the experiment:
          it sat untouched for three years because updating it was a
          chore, and now it changes whenever I ask. A longer post
          about what I delegate, what I don't, and what I've had to
          teach it is in the works.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Writing again.</strong> My last post before this
          stretch was in 2023. I'm publishing shorter pieces as they
          come, and longer posts when something earns the length.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Outside of work, I'm getting to know Chicago properly —
        neighborhoods, politics, and restaurants. I've reviewed 276
        places in this city alone; they're all on the
        <a href="/places/">Places</a> map.
      </p>

      <p class="page-note">
        This is a <a href="https://nownownow.com/about">now page</a> —
        what I'd tell a friend I haven't seen in a year.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
